     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m new to R. I previously installed R v. 3.0.3, rattle, not sure what version, and various other libraries.<br><br>I went to work through a tutorial on Sunday and saw that there was a newer version of R, so I downloaded and upgraded it, and now I&#39;m running R v. 3.1.3.<br><br>I&#39;m attempting to run rattle, but it&#39;s not. I&#39;m able to load without errors, but when I start R from the terminal, I get the following:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">R version </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2015</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">09</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">--</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Smooth Sidewalk&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Copyright</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2015</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">The</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> R </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Foundation</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Statistical</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Computing</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Platform</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</