     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Add another data point for Mr. Williams as he indicated in the FAQ since the problem wasn&#39;t with rattle, but rather with RGtk2.<div><br></div><div>Looking more closely as I tried to install from source, the compilation was failing. I needed a different version of XCode. For me, what worked was XCode 3.2.6 from around April 2011. After installing the updated XCode, RGtk2 installed from source in R by the normal, &quot;install.packages(&quot;RGtk2&quot;, type=&quot;source&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>After that, install.packages(&quot;rattle&quot;, type=&quot;source&quot;) completed successfully and then library(rattle) followed by rattle() proved it worked.</div><div><br></div><div>Maybe this can help another.</div><div><br></div><div>Have a great day!</div><div><br></div><div>--Geoffrey</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
